    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that you're supposed to say that, but it just feels so much more logical when you actually look at it. like, if a tree is diseased, you don't keep trying to water it, you just stop it from spreading. if i stay, i'm just a vessel for all this dysfunction. if i'm gone, the cycle actually has a hard stop. isn't there a kind of mercy in just stopping something before it hurts anyone else?",
